From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_NX2_OOT_SKIP_AA=1: bypass Ocarina of Time's sharpening AA network

Off unless set. Port of zortos293/Lichii PR 616 (imports #319 by ProphetWild): the prepass
(8475d671..) and the network (42593194..) are skipped and the output pass (da6df3e5..) is replaced
by a same-size point copy of the tonemap draw's B10G11R11 render target into the output pass's
target (cb0+0xd0). Lichii's per-game setting becomes the env switch; its docs, Qt strings and the
Streamline DLSS branch are left out (UsesNvidiaDlss still wins). Lichii hooks ShaderCache::
ComputeShader with DispatchReplaced, which ours lacks: here RasterizerVulkan::DispatchCompute asks
before the pipeline lookup, using a native program key LoweredNativeCode now keeps when the switch
is set. Tonemap fragment hashes compare with the salt bit ignored. Any check failing (formats,
sizes, unseen tonemap, copy refused) runs the whole network natively next frame. Unproven on PS5.
---
